- Updated Windows MDM so that an enrollment is linked to a host by the hardware serial or Autopilot device ID the device reports only when fleetd or osquery hasn't enrolled as that host yet. Otherwise, Fleet asks the host to refetch so its osquery reports and links the enrollment.
- Updated fleetd enrollment so that, with `mdm.windows_one_time_enroll_secrets` enabled, the one-time enroll secret sent with Fleet's fleetd install can't enroll as a Windows host that fleetd or osquery already enrolled as, unless that host is linked to the same MDM enrollment. Delete a re-imaged Windows host in Fleet before enrolling it in MDM again.
- Updated Windows MDM so that a host coming back from a wipe it acknowledged is treated like one coming back from a reset: fleetd's next enrollment counts as a first enrollment.
